WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:07.960
I moved in the Lower Ninth Ward in 1949.

2
00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:14.140
Our goal was to pay for our house, to educate our children, and to travel.

3
00:00:14.140 --> 00:00:20.640
And, of course, Betsy came along and interfered with all of those life plans that we had.

4
00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:24.480
We watched everything wash away.

5
00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:31.960
Suddenly we heard something under the house go [claps] boom, and I didn't know what it was.

6
00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:37.820
And so he ran back in, and he said, "Grab the kids and come on and get in the boat."

7
00:00:37.820 --> 00:00:45.560
My husband and other men who had boats stayed down here for about a week rescuing people and bringing them over to the bridge.

8
00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:50.200
And then there were a few Coast Guards that came down and rescued there.

9
00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:58.060
I don't remember the number of people that died but it was very far and in between because we still were a community.

10
00:00:58.060 --> 00:00:59.020
And people were . . . you know,

11
00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:05.820
if you would pass . . . one time one man around the corner shot a gun up to get our attention and he said,

12
00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:07.240
"Please come back and get me."

13
00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:09.260
And my husband said, "I'm going to come back."

14
00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:14.680
And so they did come back and they brought them and they went over to and put them on the bridge.

15
00:01:14.680 --> 00:01:19.340
They went to various shelters.

16
00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:24.400
We could have rode it out if it wasn't for the [levee break] explosion!

17
00:01:24.400 --> 00:01:32.480
Betsy was a crisis that really . . . that really created problems in this area.

18
00:01:32.480 --> 00:01:40.320
In some way it created problems, but in other ways it stimulated the activists.

19
00:01:40.320 --> 00:01:45.280
Because after Betsy we started fighting for urban renewal.

20
00:01:45.280 --> 00:01:53.960
We sent . . . We sent representatives to Washington [D.C.] so that we could get legislature here so that we could have some urban renewal.
